WEBVTT

00:01.820 --> 00:06.760
Alchemy, the science of understanding,
deconstructing, and reconstructing matter.

00:06.880 --> 00:09.880
However, it is not an all-powerful art.

00:10.060 --> 00:12.820
It is impossible to create
something out of nothing.

00:12.940 --> 00:17.320
If one wishes to obtain something,
something of equal value must be given.

00:17.380 --> 00:21.500
This is the law of equivalent exchange,
the basis of all alchemy.

00:21.640 --> 00:24.980
In accordance with this law,
there is a taboo among alchemists.

00:25.040 --> 00:27.580
Human transmutation is strictly forbidden.

00:27.620 --> 00:30.860
For what could equal the value
of a human soul?

00:31.280 --> 00:34.760
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

00:34.760 --> 00:37.100
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

00:38.080 --> 00:43.540
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

00:53.300 --> 00:59.540
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

00:59.860 --> 01:05.880
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

01:05.880 --> 01:12.800
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

01:12.800 --> 01:14.420
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

01:14.420 --> 01:19.580
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

01:19.580 --> 01:23.040
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

01:23.040 --> 01:26.420
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

01:26.420 --> 01:30.000
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

01:30.000 --> 01:33.140
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

01:33.140 --> 01:39.840
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

01:39.860 --> 01:44.940
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

01:44.980 --> 01:46.820
...kaeru basho mo nai no

01:46.820 --> 01:50.120
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

01:50.120 --> 01:53.600
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

01:53.600 --> 01:57.260
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

01:57.260 --> 02:00.860

02:01.400 --> 02:06.380
God's children, who live upon this land,
pray in faith and ye shall be saved.

02:06.840 --> 02:10.480
Those who have lost their way,
the Sun God Leto shall shine...

02:10.480 --> 02:13.790
So what are you guys,
like street performers or something?

02:14.200 --> 02:17.040
Seriously?! Do we look like
street performers to you?

02:17.120 --> 02:19.180
Yeah, that's why I asked!

02:19.180 --> 02:20.480
Let's go, Al.

02:20.560 --> 02:21.780
RADIO: ...I am an Emmisary of the Sun God Leto...

02:21.780 --> 02:23.780
Hey! Easy!
I didn't mean nothing by it.

02:24.780 --> 02:27.140
Sorry, accident. We'll fix it!

02:27.160 --> 02:28.760
How's that? It's smashed to hell!

02:28.890 --> 02:30.510
Watch and learn, gramps.

02:32.660 --> 02:34.390
Okay, here goes!

02:38.860 --> 02:40.440
[TWINKLING]
There, see. How's that?

02:40.520 --> 02:44.860
Amazing, it's a miracle! You've been touched
by the Sun God just like Father Cornello!

02:44.940 --> 02:46.360
Touched by who now?

02:46.360 --> 02:48.440
It's not a miracle, it's alchemy!

02:48.440 --> 02:50.820
Oh, so you two are alchemists.
Right, I've heard of them!

02:50.860 --> 02:53.460
Then maybe you've heard of us!
We're the Elric Brothers.

02:53.500 --> 02:55.160
The Elric Brothers, you say?

02:55.200 --> 02:56.920
Right...I do know that name!

02:56.920 --> 02:59.900
The Fullmetal Alchemist,
Edward Elric, is that right?

02:59.920 --> 03:03.210
[ED CHUCKLING]
Wow, so you're the young prodigy
they tell all the stories about?

03:03.300 --> 03:05.420
You've grown so much!
Look at the armor!

03:05.420 --> 03:07.540
That must be how he got
the name Fullmetal!

03:07.540 --> 03:09.780
Uh...no! Um...
It's not me!

03:09.880 --> 03:11.020
ENTIRE CROWD:
...Huh?

03:12.640 --> 03:14.880
What? You mean it's
the little guy there?

03:14.920 --> 03:18.080
Who's little?! Come here
and say that to my face I dare ya!

03:20.770 --> 03:23.800
...Lift thy voice to God...
ED: So, what's with this guy on the radio?

03:23.820 --> 03:27.320
T-That's our leader, Father Cornello.

03:27.820 --> 03:32.400
We were lost until he came to town and
began teaching us all the ways of the Sun God Leto...

03:32.400 --> 03:36.520
He grants eternal life to the souls of the faithful...
He can even resurrect the dead...

03:36.580 --> 03:39.830
His miracles are proof that
what he says is true!

03:39.920 --> 03:42.720
So this guy's claiming he
can bring the dead back to life?

03:42.980 --> 03:44.720
Now that's something I gotta see.

03:45.170 --> 03:49.760
[CROWD CHEERING]

03:54.900 --> 03:58.260
[CROWD CHEERING]
Praise Leto!

03:58.260 --> 04:01.120
ED: So that's it, huh?
What do you think?

04:01.180 --> 04:04.770
There's nothing to  think!
That's alchemy, no doubt about it.

04:05.040 --> 04:07.840
ED: But somehow he's ignoring the
law of equivalent exchange.

04:07.900 --> 04:11.760
He should've only been able to transmute
that flower into an object of equal mass.

04:11.820 --> 04:14.950
AL: And he's changing organic matter
into inorganic matter.

04:15.030 --> 04:17.220
He shouldn't be able to do that...
Unless...

04:17.240 --> 04:19.560
ED: Yeah, there's just one way...

04:19.960 --> 04:21.540
Bingo!

04:21.540 --> 04:25.600
[CHURCH BELLS RINGING]

04:30.920 --> 04:34.780
O merciful God, please hear me.
Hear my prayer, I beg of you.

04:35.550 --> 04:36.700
Please bring him back—

04:36.700 --> 04:39.260
Huh, so this is the almighty Leto?

04:39.980 --> 04:42.180
Welcome! Are you interested
in Letoism?

04:42.270 --> 04:45.340
Nope, can't say I am.
Not really the religious type.

04:46.110 --> 04:50.650
Well, I'm sorry to hear that.
To know God is to know hope.

04:50.740 --> 04:55.570
If we believe in divine grace...
Then through Him, all things are possible.

04:55.660 --> 04:57.060
If you believed...

04:57.100 --> 04:59.820
I'm sure Leto would bless you
and make you grow taller!

04:59.820 --> 05:00.040
Translation: "Sincere"
I'm sure Leto would bless you
and make you grow taller!

05:00.040 --> 05:01.780
What's that supposed to mean?!
Translation: "Sincere"

05:01.780 --> 05:03.800
Easy, brother,
she's just trying to help!
Translation: "Sincere"

05:04.120 --> 05:07.040
[SIGHS] What about bringing
the dead back to life?

05:07.620 --> 05:09.460
Do you believe that's possible, too?

05:09.550 --> 05:10.540
Yes.

05:11.240 --> 05:12.240
[SIGHS]

05:14.010 --> 05:17.220
Water, 35 liters; carbon, 20 kilograms;

05:17.300 --> 05:21.020
ammonia, 4 liters; lime, 1 .5 kilograms;

05:21.100 --> 05:23.980
phosphorus, 800 grams; salt, 250 grams;

05:24.060 --> 05:27.280
saltpeter, 100 grams, and various other trace elements.

05:27.440 --> 05:28.300
Huh?

05:30.360 --> 05:34.360
That list represents the complete chemical makeup
of the human body for the average adult.

05:34.450 --> 05:37.260
It's been calculated to
the last microgram, but still,

05:37.340 --> 05:41.020
There's never been one reported case
of successfully creating a human life.

05:41.600 --> 05:45.280
And you're telling me something modern science
can't do, you can do with prayer?!

05:45.370 --> 05:47.220
Lift thy voice to God!

05:47.460 --> 05:49.840
And the prayers of the faithful
shall be answered!

05:50.100 --> 05:52.580
Did I mention?
All those ingredients I read off...

05:52.760 --> 05:56.600
Down at the market a kid could buy every
one of them for the spare change in his pocket.

05:56.970 --> 05:59.680
As it turns out,
humans are pretty cheap.

05:59.760 --> 06:02.520
No, that's blasphemy!
People are...

06:02.560 --> 06:04.220
We are all children of God!

06:04.320 --> 06:05.820
Created in His image!

06:05.820 --> 06:06.980
[ED CHUCKLES]

06:07.200 --> 06:10.110
You have to understand,
alchemists are scientists.

06:10.190 --> 06:14.150
We don't believe in unprovable concepts
like creators or gods.

06:14.240 --> 06:16.860
We observe the physical laws
that govern this world...

06:16.950 --> 06:18.860
To try to learn the truth.

06:19.340 --> 06:20.840
It's ironic, really.

06:20.860 --> 06:24.880
That through the application of science,
we have in many ways been given the power to...

06:24.880 --> 06:26.540
[CHUCKLES]
...play gods ourselves.

06:26.540 --> 06:30.920
So you're putting yourself on the same
level as God?! That's just...sheer arrogance!

06:31.000 --> 06:33.000
You know, there's an old myth...

06:33.090 --> 06:35.700
About a hero who
flew on wings made of wax.

06:35.960 --> 06:38.900
He thought he could touch the sun,
but when he got too close...

06:38.920 --> 06:42.140
His wings melted and he came
crashing back down to Earth.

06:42.140 --> 06:43.660
Right, Al?

06:43.720 --> 06:44.680
AL: Brother...

06:45.480 --> 06:48.020
I'm sorry, Miss,
this is difficult for me to ask,

06:48.040 --> 06:52.440
But do you think your Father Cornello could
even save an arrogant scientist, like me?

06:52.580 --> 06:54.240
Of course, that's wonderful!

06:54.240 --> 06:56.920
If anyone can lead you
to the Creator's light, he can!

06:57.950 --> 07:01.410
Father Cornello, there are visitors here
who wish to see you.

07:01.490 --> 07:03.740
A child, and a man
wearing a suit of armor.

07:03.740 --> 07:06.200
They would only give their names
as "the Elric Brothers".

07:06.290 --> 07:08.780
I can't be bothered right now,
just send them away.

07:09.180 --> 07:12.200
Wait! The Elrics? You're sure that's
what they said? You're positive?

07:12.340 --> 07:14.840
Yes, Father, that's what they
called themselves. No mistake.

07:14.880 --> 07:16.720
Damn!
Then this is a problem.

07:16.720 --> 07:19.880
Edward Elric, the Fullmetal Alchemist,
has come to call on us.

07:19.970 --> 07:21.720
That's him?!
The man in the armor?

07:21.800 --> 07:23.800
Mmm. Dressing the part,
it would seem.

07:23.890 --> 07:26.600
But why would a State Alchemist
be here in Liore?

07:26.680 --> 07:29.270
Surely they can't have
found out about our plans?

07:29.350 --> 07:33.190
It's possible this dog's nose
is too sharp for his own good.

07:34.520 --> 07:36.110
This way, please.

07:36.190 --> 07:39.260
Father Cornello is a busy man,
as you can imagine.

07:39.400 --> 07:42.220
But you're in luck,
he's decided to spare a moment for you.

07:42.680 --> 07:46.160
Yeah, thanks! We understand,
we won't take too much of his time.

07:46.240 --> 07:47.490
Good, then it's agreed.

07:47.580 --> 07:49.750
We'll make this quick.

07:51.660 --> 07:54.380
Brother Cray, what is this?
What do you think you're doing?!

07:54.470 --> 07:58.590
Rose, these heathens have come to ensnare
and discredit the Father. They're evil.

07:58.670 --> 07:59.880
This is God's will.

07:59.880 --> 08:00.880
Brother Cray...!

08:01.100 --> 08:04.320
Well, like you said,
let's make this quick!

08:07.380 --> 08:08.640
[GASPS]

08:13.520 --> 08:14.980
Oh yeah, strike!

08:15.060 --> 08:17.020
What's this commotion?

08:18.940 --> 08:23.120
Ah, the Fullmetal Alchemist. Welcome
to the home of our sacred order.

08:23.600 --> 08:25.120
Father Cornello!

08:25.200 --> 08:27.840
CORNELLO: I must apologise
for my disciples' behavior.

08:27.980 --> 08:29.840
It would seem they've
been misguided.

08:29.880 --> 08:33.460
ED: Okay, let's say I believe you weren't
the one guiding them. What next?

08:33.620 --> 08:35.640
Have you come to learn
the ways of Leto?

08:35.720 --> 08:37.840
Well there are a few things
I'm curious about.

08:37.920 --> 08:41.540
Like how you've been using
second-rate alchemy to deceive your followers.

08:41.540 --> 08:42.180
[GASP]

08:42.180 --> 08:44.180
My dear boy,
I don't know what you mean.

08:44.260 --> 08:47.960
What your doubting eyes see as alchemy
are the miracles of the Sun God Leto.

08:48.880 --> 08:52.620
Look again. Could mere alchemy create
something from nothing in this way?

08:53.190 --> 08:55.240
ED: Yeah, that's
what I didn't get at first.

08:56.040 --> 08:59.880
How can you perform transmutations
that ignore the law of equivalent exchange?

08:59.880 --> 09:02.110
As I said,
because it isn't alchemy!

09:02.360 --> 09:04.400
But then I started thinking about it...

09:04.490 --> 09:08.540
If you'd somehow managed to acquire
a certain object to amplify your alchemy...

09:08.540 --> 09:11.340
One that's said to
make the impossible possible...

09:11.340 --> 09:13.290
That would explain everything.

09:13.290 --> 09:14.080
What?!

09:14.300 --> 09:17.130
I'm talking about
the Philosopher's Stone.

09:17.440 --> 09:19.460
Your ring, that's it,
isn't it?

09:21.260 --> 09:23.260
I've been looking for that.

09:23.260 --> 09:24.800
The ring is just a ring.

09:24.900 --> 09:28.640
I am God's humble servant,
it is from he alone that I derive my power.

09:28.720 --> 09:30.640
Still trying to sell that line, huh?

09:30.720 --> 09:34.810
If that's the way you wanna play it, I guess I'll have
to come up there and beat some truth out of ya.

09:34.890 --> 09:38.060
My, you really are quite
the incorrigible heathen, aren't you?

09:38.150 --> 09:39.190
Rose, dear?

09:39.270 --> 09:40.620
Yes, Father?

09:41.240 --> 09:43.360
That gun there beside you,
pick it up.

09:43.640 --> 09:45.580
Uh...O-okay?

09:47.990 --> 09:51.100
Now, child, I want you to shoot
the Fullmetal Alchemist.

09:51.140 --> 09:52.320
[GASPS]

09:52.340 --> 09:54.960
No, I...
Father I can't do that!

09:55.080 --> 10:00.200
I am the Sun God's chosen emissary.
My word is the word of Leto himself.

10:00.700 --> 10:03.380
Shoot him, Rose.
It's God's will.

10:03.480 --> 10:05.960
[SHAKY BREATHING]

10:06.010 --> 10:07.240
Why hesitate?

10:07.320 --> 10:10.500
When you lost your fiance
to that tragic accident last year,

10:10.520 --> 10:14.080
who was it that saved you
from the very depths of despair?

10:14.420 --> 10:16.080
Have you forgotten?

10:17.180 --> 10:18.840
[VOICE TREMBLING]
It was you, Father.

10:18.880 --> 10:22.520
That's right. It was I who took your
hand and lead you into God's light.

10:22.520 --> 10:24.940
And do you recall what it was
I promised you then?

10:24.960 --> 10:27.580
You said if I had faith
you'd bring him back to life!

10:29.600 --> 10:32.460
No, wait!
It's not me, honest!

10:32.460 --> 10:33.700
[GASP]

10:34.290 --> 10:36.200
Dammit,
I'm the Fullmetal Alchemist!

10:36.200 --> 10:38.180
It's not him!
It's me!

10:38.220 --> 10:40.320
It's the short one?!
You're kidding!

10:42.360 --> 10:44.840
I'm sorry, but I...
I have to do this...

10:44.840 --> 10:46.200
I don't have any choice.

10:46.400 --> 10:48.020
ED: He's been lying to you, Rose.

10:48.020 --> 10:49.800
You're wrong!
I've seen his miracles!

10:49.800 --> 10:52.390
Father Cornello will bring
him back to life, I have faith!

10:52.640 --> 10:53.800
Fine, then shoot.

11:00.060 --> 11:01.190
Al!

11:03.960 --> 11:05.420
[SHRIEKS]

11:05.490 --> 11:08.440
Good. God Leto is pleased,
you have done well, my child.

11:08.440 --> 11:10.860
Now pick up the gun and
shoot the other as well.

11:11.640 --> 11:13.830
Haven't you made her do
enough already?

11:13.910 --> 11:14.910
[GASPS]

11:15.040 --> 11:17.450
But...your head...!
I thought you were...

11:17.540 --> 11:19.300
Don't worry about it,
he's pretty solid.

11:19.300 --> 11:21.140
Yeah, see?
No harm done.

11:23.090 --> 11:25.700
An empty suit of armor that
walks and speaks!

11:25.700 --> 11:27.540
Do you still doubt it, Rose?

11:27.540 --> 11:29.640
This unholy thing is an abomination!

11:29.660 --> 11:31.840
Evil of this kind must be purged!

11:35.120 --> 11:37.040
[GROWLING]

11:37.120 --> 11:40.240
And I believe my Chimera
should be up to the task.

11:40.980 --> 11:44.740
So this is the sorta thing you do with
a Philosopher's Stone? That's just twisted.

11:44.740 --> 11:45.920
[GASP]

11:46.360 --> 11:49.990
Anyway, looks like I'll need a weapon.

11:56.620 --> 11:58.520
No transmutation circle?!

11:58.560 --> 12:02.240
So the State Alchemist title
isn't just for show, you truly are gifted.

12:02.260 --> 12:03.540
However...!

12:03.800 --> 12:05.540
[CHIMERA ROARS]

12:07.960 --> 12:11.720
Your little spear is no match for
Chimera claws that tear through iron!

12:12.640 --> 12:14.760
You shredded my pants.

12:17.360 --> 12:20.540
But I guess those claws don't do
so good against steel!

12:20.660 --> 12:22.640
Bite him, you stupid beast!

12:25.980 --> 12:30.500
You like that, kitty?
Go on, get a good taste!

12:35.060 --> 12:36.580
Your arm...

12:36.600 --> 12:38.740
A brother trapped in armor...

12:38.900 --> 12:41.860
I see. It's all
becoming clear now.

12:42.340 --> 12:43.980
You did it, didn't you?

12:44.000 --> 12:48.170
The one thing even the most novice
alchemist knows is strictly forbidden!

12:48.250 --> 12:50.210
Why don't you come down
here and try me?

12:50.300 --> 12:52.860
I'll show you real quick
who the novice is!

12:53.500 --> 12:55.060
Fullmetal Alchemist.

12:57.000 --> 12:58.780
Fullmetal Alchemist.

12:59.600 --> 13:01.420
Why don't you come down
here and try me?

13:01.420 --> 13:03.800
I'll show you real quick
who the novice is!

13:03.800 --> 13:06.460
Rose...
this is the price of their sin.

13:06.460 --> 13:08.880
These fools attempted
human transmutation,

13:08.880 --> 13:11.280
the greatest taboo
for any alchemist!

13:11.660 --> 13:15.440
In their arrogance, they tried to
bring someone dead back to life.

13:16.500 --> 13:22.600
He thought he could touch the sun, but when he got too close
his wings melted and he came crashing back down to Earth.

13:23.330 --> 13:24.660
Oh, no...

13:24.750 --> 13:28.980
This is what happens when you try to
play God, or whatever you wanna call it.

13:29.170 --> 13:32.380
Take a good look, Rose.
Is this what you want?

13:33.240 --> 13:38.460
So this is the great Fullmetal Alchemist,
Edward Elric, not even half a man.

13:38.460 --> 13:39.920
Hell, not even half a boy!

13:39.960 --> 13:41.360
And what are you?!

13:41.380 --> 13:44.620
You're just a phony that can't do
anything without a Philosopher's Stone!

13:44.620 --> 13:48.270
Father, we just want you to hand
over the Stone before you get hurt.

13:48.640 --> 13:49.960
Don't be absurd!

13:49.960 --> 13:52.580
Why? So you could use it
for yourself? Please.

13:52.740 --> 13:57.440
If you fools are really so eager to play God,
then perhaps I should send you to meet him instead!

14:01.280 --> 14:01.960
Huh?

14:02.290 --> 14:05.480
Nah, me and God,
we don't get along too well.

14:05.500 --> 14:08.940
Even if I went, he'd probably
just send me right back here.

14:12.580 --> 14:14.170
[ROSE SCREAMS]

14:14.170 --> 14:15.090
This way!

14:22.640 --> 14:24.540
Well don't just stand there!
After them!

14:24.560 --> 14:27.940
These heathens seek to harm the order!
They must be stopped!

14:31.040 --> 14:32.120
That's far enough.

14:32.120 --> 14:34.720
What are you gonna do, boy?
You're unarmed and outnumbered.

14:35.000 --> 14:37.860
Look, just come quietly.
We don't wanna have to rough you up.

14:38.380 --> 14:39.320
Ha ha ha ha!

14:41.160 --> 14:41.740
Huh?!

14:41.740 --> 14:43.480
[ALL SCREAMING]

14:44.790 --> 14:47.040
Don't go easy just 'cause
he's a kid, you got that?

14:47.830 --> 14:49.670
[YELLING]

14:50.440 --> 14:52.620
[ED CACKLING]

14:53.590 --> 14:55.960
AL: What do you think of
Cornello now, Rose?

14:57.050 --> 15:00.160
He just opened fire, he didn't
care that you were in the way.

15:00.180 --> 15:02.390
But...that's because...

15:05.140 --> 15:07.460
What he said back there
is true, isn't it?

15:09.000 --> 15:13.740
We're not evil. All we wanted was
to see our mom smile again.

15:14.660 --> 15:17.360
But our transmutation failed.

15:17.450 --> 15:20.660
What we made...
wasn't even human.

15:22.820 --> 15:25.180
We learned our
mistake the hard way.

15:25.600 --> 15:29.040
People don't come back
from the dead. Not ever.

15:29.330 --> 15:31.370
That's not true!
I mean...

15:31.460 --> 15:34.670
Alchemy is based on
the law of equivalent exchange.

15:34.750 --> 15:38.660
The price of even a failed
human transmutation was enormous.

15:39.140 --> 15:44.320
It cost my brother his left leg,
and it cost me my whole body.

15:45.360 --> 15:48.820
Do you see it?
My brother drew that with his own blood.

15:49.380 --> 15:50.440
[GASP]

15:51.100 --> 15:55.720
His leg had been taken, he was bleeding,
I can't imagine the pain he was in...

15:55.820 --> 15:59.860
But through all that he still gave up his
right arm to transmute my soul...

15:59.900 --> 16:02.540
and bonded me
to this suit of armor.

16:04.520 --> 16:08.300
Now, I just want to help him get his
body back to the way it was.

16:08.800 --> 16:11.960
He wants to find a way to get
me back to normal, too.

16:12.140 --> 16:15.800
It won't be easy.
We might even get killed along the way.

16:16.820 --> 16:20.920
But that's the path we chose.
All we can do is keep moving.

16:21.010 --> 16:23.680
But, Father Cornello said...

16:23.960 --> 16:24.740
[GASP]

16:25.390 --> 16:27.340
He said he could do it,
he promised me!

16:27.340 --> 16:30.020
Just because you and your brother
failed that doesn't mean...

16:30.220 --> 16:31.770
It doesn't mean he will!

16:34.770 --> 16:36.780
There you are,
you infernal brat!

16:36.920 --> 16:39.480
Look, can we just cut
the crap and talk here?

16:39.570 --> 16:42.860
All I want are some straight
answers about the Stone.

16:43.280 --> 16:46.040
Tell me what I need to know,
and I'll be on my way.

16:46.220 --> 16:48.160
Or we could get the
military involved...?

16:50.920 --> 16:52.660
Ask your questions.

16:52.750 --> 16:55.480
You could do anything with a
Philosopher's Stone, right?

16:55.480 --> 16:58.680
So why waste all that power
performing phony miracles?

17:00.040 --> 17:03.320
Because with each miracle I can attract
new believers to the order.

17:03.320 --> 17:06.160
Believers who would
lay down their lives for my sake!

17:06.300 --> 17:08.040
I'm slowly building an army...

17:08.040 --> 17:10.940
A legion of holy warriors,
unafraid to die!

17:11.260 --> 17:15.540
In a few more years, I'll be ready to unleash
this mindless horde upon the world!

17:15.620 --> 17:19.020
And I'll use the Philosopher's Stone
to tear this country apart.

17:19.260 --> 17:22.380
Who knows?
I might even carve out a slice for you.

17:22.380 --> 17:23.840
[CACKLING]

17:24.200 --> 17:27.560
[ED JOINS LAUGHING]
CORNELLO: Wait, what are you  laughing about?

17:27.560 --> 17:30.760
I knew it! You really
are a novice, aren't you?

17:37.210 --> 17:38.140
[GASPS]

17:38.220 --> 17:40.560
You don't mean that—?!

17:41.000 --> 17:43.300
There were never
any miracles, Rose.

17:43.300 --> 17:45.860
He lied to you.
He lied to everyone.

17:46.200 --> 17:48.120
CORNELLO: Why, you...!

17:48.120 --> 17:50.480
How long?!
How long has that been on?!

17:50.890 --> 17:52.140
ED: From the start!

17:52.220 --> 17:54.140
Your believers heard every word.

17:54.230 --> 17:56.020
CORNELLO: How could you?!

17:56.360 --> 17:58.360
You'll pay dearly for this!

17:59.190 --> 18:00.980
Sorry, not today!

18:02.610 --> 18:05.380
Just face it,
you're outclassed here.

18:07.660 --> 18:09.570
I am without rival!

18:18.940 --> 18:20.620
I-It's a rebound!

18:20.640 --> 18:23.380
No! I won't be disgraced like this!

18:23.700 --> 18:26.440
Now boy... behold...

18:26.460 --> 18:29.860
[VOICE DISTORTING]
...the chosen emissary of the Sun God Leto!

18:49.700 --> 18:55.250
My word is the divine word of God himself!
My fist is the almighty fist of judgement!

18:55.620 --> 18:56.860
Oh yeah?

18:57.000 --> 18:58.860
Fist of God, huh?

19:00.400 --> 19:02.960
Well if that's what you want,
you can have it!

19:19.000 --> 19:20.560
[GROANING]

19:20.880 --> 19:22.060
Shut up!

19:22.500 --> 19:24.580
Just give me the
Philosopher's Stone!

19:29.560 --> 19:31.080
What the hell...?

19:31.520 --> 19:32.950
The Stone...

19:32.960 --> 19:37.040
It's supposed to be perfect material...
How did it just break like that?!

19:37.240 --> 19:40.160
I-I don't know.
I don't know anything about it!

19:40.160 --> 19:43.560
S-Spare me! Please! I-I was wrong!
Please, I beg you!

19:43.560 --> 19:45.200
It's a damn fake.

19:45.200 --> 19:49.040
Please, don't! I'm helpless without
the Stone. Spare me, please!

19:49.040 --> 19:50.740
You mean we
went through all this...

19:50.740 --> 19:53.260
Risked our lives for this
one possible chance...

19:53.400 --> 19:55.720
and it's a fake?!

19:55.820 --> 19:58.580
So u-uh...
what about me?

19:59.680 --> 20:02.400
I don't care what you do,
just get outta here!

20:02.400 --> 20:03.400
Right!

20:06.260 --> 20:08.030
AL: And what about the Stone?

20:08.110 --> 20:10.610
ED: Phony, just like him.

20:10.700 --> 20:11.740
AL: Oh.

20:13.070 --> 20:16.880
I'm sorry, Al. For awhile there I thought
we'd really found a way to get your body back.

20:17.080 --> 20:19.460
ROSE: Give me the Philosopher's Stone!

20:20.080 --> 20:21.480
AL: Rose...

20:22.580 --> 20:25.960
Like I was just saying, it was a fake.
It wasn't real.

20:26.240 --> 20:28.020
Besides, it's shattered now.

20:28.020 --> 20:30.780
Liar! You wanna keep it for
yourself, don't you?!

20:31.090 --> 20:33.760
So you can use it on your bodies!
That's right!

20:33.760 --> 20:36.140
And so you can try to bring
your mother back again!

20:36.160 --> 20:37.700
You shut up!

20:38.220 --> 20:42.300
People don't come back from
the dead, Rose. Not ever.

20:44.060 --> 20:45.520
Not ever.

20:47.560 --> 20:49.860
But he promised me...

20:50.360 --> 20:52.740
He said if I prayed it
would happen...

20:52.780 --> 20:54.880
[CRYING]
...a miracle...

20:56.180 --> 21:00.440
That hope was all I had left,
what am I supposed to believe in now?!

21:00.980 --> 21:02.910
Tell me what to do!

21:03.960 --> 21:05.200
Please!

21:06.980 --> 21:10.320
I can't tell you that,
you have to figure it out.

21:11.920 --> 21:16.020
Stand up and walk.
Keep moving forward.

21:16.540 --> 21:19.320
You've got two good legs,
so use them.

21:20.420 --> 21:23.060
You're strong enough to
make your own path.

21:29.680 --> 21:33.100
Bring him out here!
We're through listening to those lies!

21:33.100 --> 21:36.180
Show yourself! Just get out here!
Open up!

21:37.990 --> 21:40.820
That damn brat, it's all all ruined!
Everything I worked for!

21:40.830 --> 21:42.980
Yes, all that hard work for nothing.

21:42.980 --> 21:43.540
Huh?!

21:43.540 --> 21:46.370
I knew we should've just
incited a little rebellion.

21:47.220 --> 21:48.060
You...!

21:48.080 --> 21:51.840
I'm hungry, Lust, can I eat the old man?
Please, he's big and fat!

21:51.840 --> 21:56.100
Not this one, Gluttony.
We don't want you giving yourself indigestion.

21:56.340 --> 21:58.620
Now you too?
Everyone has mocked me!

21:58.620 --> 22:00.240
I won't stand for—

22:04.840 --> 22:07.650
I'd say this concludes
our business.

22:11.980 --> 22:14.780
Just as things were beginning
to look promising, too.

22:14.780 --> 22:17.360
Now I suppose we'll have to
start over from scratch.

22:18.100 --> 22:19.880
Father won't be pleased.

22:20.180 --> 22:24.240
In any case, it's time we started
thinking about our next move.

22:26.660 --> 22:27.740
[CRUNCH]

22:28.380 --> 22:34.200
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

22:34.280 --> 22:39.500
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

22:39.560 --> 22:45.260
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

22:45.520 --> 22:50.400
futari yorisotta

22:53.480 --> 22:58.660
Muri na egao no ura

22:58.660 --> 23:04.040
nobita kage o kakumau

23:04.080 --> 23:13.420
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

23:15.500 --> 23:22.640
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

23:26.060 --> 23:31.480
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

23:31.480 --> 23:35.780
zenbu wakatte'tan da

23:35.860 --> 23:41.340
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

23:41.340 --> 23:46.540
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

23:46.540 --> 23:51.980
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

23:52.220 --> 23:57.040
futari arukidasu

24:00.840 --> 24:06.760
Following the incident in Liore, Ed and Al travel to
the Eastern Command Center to report to Colonel Mustang.

24:06.820 --> 24:11.380
Once there, they are taken to the home
of the Sewing Life Alchemist, Shou Tucker,

24:11.400 --> 24:16.000
and his young daughter, Nina, where they hope
to learn more about the field of bio-alchemy.

24:16.400 --> 24:19.460
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:19.500 --> 24:22.940
Episode 4: An Alchemist's Anguish

24:23.700 --> 24:27.870
Some meetings in this life
are destined only for heartbreak.
